{"ticker":"NEE","updated":"2026-10-23T23:22:01Z","profile":{"longName":"NextEra Energy, Inc.","shortName":"NextEra Energy, Inc.","sector":"Utilities","industry":"Utilities - Regulated Electric","country":"United States","website":"https://www.nexteraenergy.com","fullTimeEmployees":17400,"marketCap":172188827648,"trailingPE":14.792792,"forwardPE":18.751526,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":5.973593,"pegRatio":1.67,"targetMeanPrice":94.57895,"targetHighPrice":110.0,"targetLowPrice":56.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":19,"recommendationKey":"buy","revenueGrowth":0.016,"earningsGrowth":0.932,"grossMargins":0.60173,"operatingMargins":0.33004,"profitMargins":0.40370998,"totalRevenue":28824999936,"beta":0.639,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":98.75,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":74.41,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":3.04},"summary":"NextEra Energy, Inc., through its subsidiaries, generates, stores, transmits, distributes, and sells electric power to retail and wholesale customers in North America. It operates through Florida Power & Light Company (FPL) and NEER segments. The company generates electricity from wind, solar, nuclear, natural gas, and other clean energy assets. It also invests in generation, storage, transmission, and distribution facilities; owns, develops, constructs, manages, and operates generation facilities, including renewables, nuclear and natural gas, and battery storage facilities in the wholesale energy market in the United States and Canada, as well as electric and gas transmission assets, and natural gas pipelines; provides full energy and capacity requirement services; markets and trades in energy-related commodities; and participates in the production of natural gas, natural gas liquids, and oil. As of December 31, 2025, the company had approximately 35,963 megawatts of net generating capacity; approximately 93,000 circuit miles of transmission and distribution lines; and 932 substations. It serves approximately 12 million people through approximately 6 million customer accounts on the east and lower west coasts of Florida. The company was formerly known as FPL Group, Inc. and changed its name to NextEra Energy, Inc. in 2010. NextEra Energy, Inc. was founded in 1925 and is headq","summary_zh":"NextEra Energy, Inc. 透過其子公司為北美的零售和批發客戶生產、儲存、傳輸、分配和銷售電力。它透過佛羅裡達電力與照明公司 (FPL) 和 NEER 部門運作。該公司利用風能、太陽能、核能、天然氣和其他清潔能源資產發電。它還投資發電、儲存、輸電和配電設施；擁有、開發、建造、管理和營運發電設施，包括美國和加拿大批發能源市場的再生能源、核能和天然氣以及電池儲存設施，以及電力和天然氣傳輸資產以及天然氣管道；提供全面的能源和容量需求服務；能源相關商品的市場和貿易；並參與天然氣、液化天然氣和石油管道的生產。截至2025年12月31日，公司淨發電量約為35,963兆瓦；約 93,000 英里的輸電和配電線路；和932個變電站。它透過佛羅裡達州東海岸和下西海岸的約 600 萬個客戶帳戶為約 1200 萬人提供服務。該公司前身為 FPL Group, Inc.，於 2010 年更名為 NextEra Energy, Inc.。 NextEra Energy, Inc. 成立於 1925 年，總部為","sector_zh":"公用事業","industry_zh":"公用事業 - 受監管的電力","candles":[{"t":"2025-08-25","o":75.81,"h":76.2,"l":75.11,"c":75.32,"v":6337700},{"t":"2025-08-26","o":75.44,"h":75.75,"l":74.43,"c":74.84,"v":7162700},{"t":"2025-08-27","o":74.91,"h":75.01,"l":73.4,"c":73.89,"v":10119000},{"t":"2025-08-28","o":73.26,"h":73.48,"l":71.9,"c":72.09,"v":10917200},{"t":"2025-08-29","o":72.4,"h":72.83,"l":71.82,"c":72.05,"v":11280500},{"t":"2025-09-02","o":72.27,"h":72.66,"l":71.49,"c":72.65,"v":8661500},{"t":"2025-09-03","o":72.12,"h":72.63,"l":71.36,"c":71.63,"v":7722300},{"t":"2025-09-04","o":72.05,"h":72.5,"l":70.16,"c":70.87,"v":14596800},{"t":"2025-09-05","o":71.25,"h":71.73,"l":70.26,"c":70.9,"v":10067600},{"t":"2025-09-08","o":70.83,"h":70.84,"l":69.24,"c":69.77,"v":12596500},{"t":"2025-09-09","o":69.66,"h":70.32,"l":69.54,"c":70.07,"v":7294500},{"t":"2025-09-10","o":70.0,"h":71.33,"l":69.62,"c":71.04,"v":9254400},{"t":"2025-09-11","o":70.97,"h":71.44,"l":70.51,"c":71.32,"v":7418300},{"t":"2025-09-12","o":71.15,"h":72.49,"l":70.81,"c":71.64,"v":9345600},{"t":"2025-09-15","o":71.58,"h":72.2,"l":71.3,"c":71.5,"v":10399100},{"t":"2025-09-16","o":71.29,"h":71.54,"l":69.77,"c":69.83,"v":7930200},{"t":"2025-09-17","o":70.28,"h":71.01,"l":70.1,"c":70.31,"v":10799600},{"t":"2025-09-18","o":